Package: nexus-desktop
Version: @VERSION@-@RELEASE@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Nexus Contributors <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-pyside6.qtcore (>= 6.8), python3-pyside6.qtgui (>= 6.8), python3-pyside6.qtwidgets (>= 6.8), python3-pyside6.qtnetwork (>= 6.8), libqt6svg6, qt6-svg-plugins, qt6-qpa-plugins, fonts-dejavu-core
Recommends: qt6-wayland
Suggests: nexus-engine
Homepage: https://github.com/luen-eth/Nexus
Description: Desktop interface for local Nexus AI models
 Select local GGUF models, manage an inference server, and inspect its status in a
 native Qt desktop interface. No model weights or native engine binary are
 included in this architecture-independent GUI package.
 .
 Requires distribution PySide6 packages, available in Debian 13 and Ubuntu
 26.04 universe. Install a separately compatible Nexus engine or connect to
 an existing local server. This package is not an Arch Linux package.
